The Evolution Data Server package provides a unified backend for programs that work with
contacts, tasks, and calendar information. It was originally developed for Evolution
(hence the name), but is now used by other packages as well. 

The Evolution Data Server provides a single database for common, desktop-wide information,
such as a user's address book or calendar events.

By using the evolution-data-server, other GNOME applications are integrating with Evolution.

  * gnome-panel calendar applet lists your appointments and tasks.
  * Synchronize your Pidgin buddies with your Evolution contacts.
  * View Planner files as Evolution task lists.


===========================
S/MIME TRIPLE-WRAP FORK
===========================

This branch (triple-wrap) is a personal, experimental fork. It is not
affiliated with the upstream Evolution Data Server project; everything above
this section is the original upstream README.

Its only change to Camel is a Content-Description on the S/MIME signature part,
in src/camel/camel-smime-context.c, matching what camel_gpg_context already
sets on the signature part it builds.

The RFC 2634 S/MIME triple-wrapping itself needs no change to Camel and is
implemented entirely in Evolution. See the triple-wrap branch of

    https://github.com/mward5/evolution

for what it does, how to build it, which parts of RFC 2634 it does and does not
implement, and the design.
